WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.550
WHO's Francesco Branca says calls for
responsible food marketing have not had

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.470
a meaningful impact.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.050
Chile went further.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:14.750
From 2016, many packaged foods carried
black warning labels on the front.

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.610
Advertising them to children was limited,

6
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.910
and schools could not sell
foods over set limits.

7
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.390
So did Chilean families buy less?

8
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.750
Or did they just ignore the labels?

9
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.137
In this mission, you'll meet the
players who shape what we eat:

10
00:00:28.187 --> 00:00:33.690
UN agencies, governments, NG Os
and transnational corporations.

11
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.270
Then you'll evaluate the
evidence on Chile's law,

12
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.810
and the gender gaps in who
grows, buys and eats food.

13
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.510
Your mission: evaluate whether Chile's
warning labels and advertising limits made

14
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.070
families buy less.
